7.4},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","change":"Burlington's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","rain":"Burlington has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 39\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>39\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 47\u00b0F, and the record is 65\u00b0F (1885, 2012). The low of <strong>31\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Burlington's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Burlington has set <strong class=\"sig\">18 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 72 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">144 record highs</strong>, far more than the 70 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). Burlington's all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on August 11, 1944.","t_chg":"Burlington's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 133 complete years: Burlington's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.02 to +0.22), about +1.6\u00b0F since 1892. Burlington's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.33\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.25 to +0.40), about +4.3\u00b0F since 1892.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Burlington has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Burlington's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.55 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.33 to +0.76), about +7.7 inches since 1884. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 37.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (50.92 in); the driest, 1894 (21.31 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}